WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.540
After his debut in Daredevil Season 2, Jon
Bernthal's Punisher was such a huge hit that

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.680
he got his own series and at the end of the
last episode of The Defenders, there's a cool

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.540
post-credits teaser for Frank Castle's new
solo show.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.090
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I'll be breaking down the

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:21.179
new Punisher teaser for easter eggs and clues
on what we can expect from Jon Bernthal's

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:22.179
upcoming series.

00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:26.689
Also, I'm running a Punisher and Defenders
giveaway, so make sure you subscribe and leave

00:00:26.689 --> 00:00:30.519
a comment for a chance to win a Punisher or
Defenders Funko Pop.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:34.910
As Jon Bernthal previously revealed in an
EW interview, The Punisher series will heavily

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.059
feature Frank Castle's military background.

00:00:37.059 --> 00:00:41.579
And, true to this, the new teaser shows quite
a bit more of Castle's military past with

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:45.780
heavy hints at some serious conflicts he got
into during his time in the forces.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.420
You can see his fist here smash the photo
of himself with his colleagues and there's

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.019
another shot later where Castle is being held
back from assaulting this guy.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:57.720
And, if you look closely, it seems like Castle
has given him a nasty injury to his left eye.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.931
I suspect this could be the character William
Rawlins who is played by Paul Schulze, an

00:01:01.931 --> 00:01:06.270
actor best known for roles in Nurse Jackie,
24, and The Sopranos.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.970
In the comics, Rawlins was a crooked CIA agent
who engineered various terrorist attacks and

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.250
deliberately abandoned his wife Kathryn O'Brien
in Afghanistan.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:19.820
Later, O'Brien and Castle captured Rawlins
who lost an eye while being interrogated by

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:20.820
Castle.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.530
And there's another shot in the teaser of
Rawlins with what looks like either a glass

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:28.070
or injured left eye confirming that some aspect
of this comic book story will likely play

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.000
out in The Punisher.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.910
Comic-book Rawlins also had a hand in drug
smuggling, so I wonder if The Punisher series

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:38.290
will give us any links between him and Colonel
Schoonover, Castle's former Commanding Officer

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.970
who turned out to be a major drug lord in
Daredevil Season 2.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.200
The teaser also gives us a glimpse at what
looks like Castle's wife being shot.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.410
Actress Kelli Barrett has been cast in the
role of Frank's wife, Maria Castle.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:54.660
Maria looked rather different in the photos
of Frank's family in Daredevil Season 2, so

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.380
it seems safe to say that her character's
been recast for The Punisher.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.560
What's even more interesting though is that
if this is Maria being shot in her home, this

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.540
could conflict with the story established
in Daredevil.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:10.440
In the tenth episode of season 2, DA Samantha
Reyes confessed that Frank Castle's family

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:15.500
was killed in Central Park when a sting operation
against various gangs went wrong and Castle's

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.470
wife and children were fatally injured in
the crossfire.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.080
So, what does this mean for Maria?

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.730
Well, either there's something not completely
true about DA Reyes' story or perhaps the

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.870
shot in the teaser is a fake-out, either a
warning or threat to Frank from someone like

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.540
Rawlins, or even perhaps a hallucination or
nightmare in Castle's mind.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.260
Either way, according to IMDB, Maria is set
to appear in 7 episodes and her children in

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.880
four, so it looks like we'll get to see Castle
spend some time with his family in the new

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:46.790
show, for example this shot of him with his
children, sailing past the Statue of Liberty.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:50.960
Indeed, speaking with EW, Bernthal said that
'the Frank Castle that was in Daredevil is

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:55.810
not in Punisher', so the fact this teaser
shows us that we'll see more of what made

00:02:55.810 --> 00:03:00.130
Castle the Punisher, in other words, his relationship
with his family and their fate, as well as

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.070
his military past, ties in well with that.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:07.100
And during a recent interview with Moviefone,
Bernthal talked about taking pains to make

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.560
sure Castle wasn't depicted as too 'heroic'
in the new series.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.820
For Bernthal, it was crucial to get across
just how 'brutal, […] damaged, […and]

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.820
tortured' Frank is, and he wanted to make
sure they explored his 'pain and what's behind

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.180
the violence and the reason he's committing
[it]'.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:26.140
Speaking of pain and torture, it's not 100%
clear in this scene exactly who's being tortured.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.520
Could it be Castle, perhaps in retaliation
for what he did to Rawlins?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.700
Though the guy's profile doesn't quite look
like Bernthal's to me.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.100
Or could it be showing that Castle's taken
part in torturing this man?

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.100
What do you think?

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.540
Jon Bernthal's voiceover in this teaser is
also really interesting as it suggests that

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.760
The Punisher series is going to delve much
deeper into Frank Castle's psyche.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.709
In the voiceover, Castle talks about having
made a deal with the devil, which ties in

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:53.350
with Punisher's origin story as told by Garth
Ennis in his four-part comic book miniseries

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.350
"Born".

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:57.910
In that story, it was a voice inside Castle's
head which helped him deal with the horrors

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.010
of the Vietnam War.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.350
And that voice which talks to Frank in the
miniseries may represent either the devil

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.400
or death.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.330
In fact, there's a chilling page in the final
issue where, after Frank returns home, he

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:12.770
sees a picture of his own family framed inside
an outline of the Punisher skull, and an inner

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.209
voice reminds him that there's a price to
pay.

00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:19.209
This links nicely to the line in the teaser
where Frank says "he's coming, he's coming

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:20.549
to collect".

00:04:20.549 --> 00:04:25.330
That line not only foreshadows how Frank lost
his family after returning from the war, but

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.400
it also teases the vigilante justice we can
expect to see Punisher dispatching to the

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.009
criminal underworld in his new series.

00:04:32.009 --> 00:04:36.150
As for the repeated image of Frank sledgehammering
a concrete floor, this seems like it could

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.660
just be footage for the teaser trailer, although
it does make me think of the scene in the

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:43.699
first John Wick movie where he uses a sledge
hammer to break out his stash of weapons and

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:47.150
gold to go on the rampage against the criminals
who wronged him.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.909
So, what did you think of the teaser for The
Punisher?

00:04:49.909 --> 00:04:52.710
And has it got you hyped for the upcoming
full season on Netflix?

